/*
  core/stressors/external_distraction.spthy -- f_U for sigma2 ExternalDistraction, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC.

  Migrated to the agnostic interface (AGNOSTIC_STRESSOR_INTERFACE.md). sigma2 is the ACTION-GENERIC
  stressor: distraction can strike during ANY pending step, so it inspects no field. The old rule read
  any !Req(P,_,_,_,_) merely to bind a party with work in hand; this version reads any !Step(P,_,_)
  -- action a free variable, NO !Demands constraint -- so it binds on any interaction step in the
  agnostic Layer-1 vocabulary and names no ceremony fact. It is the one detector that reads !Step
  WITHOUT consulting the lexicon, precisely because the construct is action-independent.

  Wickens' Multiple Resource Theory (2008): a competing channel/task degrades performance regardless
  of the primary task. At onset emits SetMask(P,'Careless') -- everything below SetMask is UNCHANGED.
  !StressEnable(P) gates per party (Stage B); OneDistractPerParty caps it to one onset per party.
*/

rule Trigger_ExternalDistraction:
    [ !Step(P, sid, action), !StressEnable(P) ]
  --[ Distract(P), SetMask(P,'Careless') ]->
    [ ]

restriction OneDistractPerParty:
  "All p #i #j. Distract(p)@i & Distract(p)@j ==> #i = #j"
